/-!
# Cerberus Core

The Core syntax of the Cerberus C semantics at `rems-project/cerberus@b3e11ea3`,
written by hand from `frontend/model/core.lem` and the Lem types it reaches, in
Silmaril's naming conventions. `Names` maps each Cerberus name to its Silmaril name.
Argument order follows the Lem declarations. Lem maps are `Map`, a `Finmap` keyed
by Lem's key equality. Memory-model values are parameters of `MemoryModel`,
because Cerberus implements them in OCaml.

`Schema` checks structural agreement for 60 variants and four records through
`Names`, with coverage of all 81 pinned Lem entries in `Schema.Generated`. Every
target must name a Lean type. Abstract and abbreviated representations and payload
types are not compared.

`Codec.WellFormed.parseDocument` decodes canonical tagged S-expressions into a
`Codec.Document`. It retains wire bindings for byte-for-byte re-encoding and
constructs the semantic `Core.File` using `Map.ofList`. Its errors include child
paths; its well-formedness pass checks digest length and Lem map ordering.
-/
